From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charlie <5764343+charlielye@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:22:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] refactor: read the canonical genesis from
 @aztec-foundation/protocol-genesis

The canonical genesis (its inputs and the roots they produce) is published by the
protocol release as @aztec-foundation/protocol-genesis, measured by barretenberg's
reference world state. Labs reads every genesis value from it:

- protocol-contracts takes DEFAULT_GENESIS_DATA's prefilled nullifiers, public data
  and timestamp from the package's inputs; the generator no longer computes them.
- world-state builds its Init message (tree heights, prefill sizes, header
  generator point) from the package's inputs.
- stdlib exports GENESIS_BLOCK_HEADER_HASH, GENESIS_NULLIFIER_TREE_ROOT and
  GENESIS_ARCHIVE_ROOT from the package's outputs. @aztec-labs/constants no longer
  carries them; they are no longer protocol constants.

genesis_data.test.ts now checks the package's nullifiers against a TS derivation
from the bundled protocol artifacts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015HXzMEGRnmFYs5yXRcAWCb

